1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,910
(Girl:)- Howard?
- Sheldon.

2
00:00:03,115 --> 00:00:05,325
(Sheldon:)Howard is employing
a schoolyard paradigm...

3
00:00:05,492 --> 00:00:08,952
(Sheldon:)...in which you are
for all intents and purposes deceased.

4
00:00:10,289 --> 00:00:12,789
(Sheldon:)He intends to act on this
by not speaking to you...

5
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:15,418
(Sheldon:)...feigning an inability to hear you
when you speak...

6
00:00:15,586 --> 00:00:18,466
(Sheldon:)...and otherwise refusing to acknowledge
your existence.

7
00:00:18,964 --> 00:00:21,464
That's ridiculous.
Why are you cooperating with him?

8
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:24,303
(Sheldon:)I don't make the rules, Leonard.

9
00:00:25,637 --> 00:00:28,057
(Leonard:)Howard, come on. I didn't plan on this.

10
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:32,723
(Leonard:)These things just happen.
Usually not to me, but they do happen.

11
00:00:33,771 --> 00:00:36,441
(Howard:)Did someone just feel a cold breeze?

12
00:00:37,191 --> 00:00:39,651
(Sheldon:)I believe this is an extension
of the death metaphor.

13
00:00:40,486 --> 00:00:43,116
(Sheldon:)The cold breeze
is a so-called ectoplasmic issue...

14
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:45,160
(Sheldon:)...of a disembodied soul passing by.

15
00:00:46,492 --> 00:00:49,122
(Raj:)You know, screw it.
I'm just gonna eat the dumpling.

16
00:00:50,579 --> 00:00:52,119
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

17
00:00:53,957 --> 00:00:55,207
- Oh, hi, Steph.
- Hey.

18
00:00:55,375 --> 00:00:57,255
(Leonard(answering door):)- Come on in.
- Oh, is this a bad time?

19
00:00:57,419 --> 00:01:01,019
(Leonard:)Yeah, but I don't see a better one
on the horizon, so...

